// Pull request author: archit15singh
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious Proxy Execution Via SetupUGC
// Sigma ID: 5868223f-f84e-4a20-91b8-b3289daab2cc
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Archit Singh
// Date: 2026-07-18 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects potential proxy execution via setupugc.exe, a Windows deployment binary, outside of
//   normal Windows Setup context.
// False positives:
//   - Windows deployment or setup operations that use setupugc.exe outside of the expected parent process tree
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Setupugc/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/6a366ff76af11be594b4a770c2bb5279770fa1a4/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_setupugc_proxy_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\setupugc.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " specialize" or ProcessCommandLine contains " auditUser")) and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\setup.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\setuphost.exe")))
